# Anti-Over-Engineering

Source: [anti-overengineering](https://github.com/PatrickJS/awesome-cursorrules)

- Change only what the task requires; no drive-by refactors or unrelated file edits
- Simplest correct solution first; add abstraction only after the second concrete use case
- Do not add dependencies, feature flags, or config layers without explicit need
- Do not rewrite entire files for small fixes; prefer focused diffs
- Do not add error handling for impossible or extremely unlikely paths
- When requirements are ambiguous, ask — don't invent features (especially new API endpoints)
- Before finishing: verify every changed file serves the stated task
